# Hide my API Keys
    .env
    
    # Hide massive AI Weights and Datasets
    *.pth
    *.pt
    data/graph_data/
    data/processed/
    
    # Hide Python junk
    __pycache__/
    ```
  
  
    Make sure your terminal is standing in your main `dopant-discovery-gnn` folder. Run these commands one by one:
    1. `git init` *(This turns your folder into a Git repository)*
    2. `git add .` *(This stages all your safe files to be saved)*
    3. `git commit -m "Initial commit: GNN Active Learning Pipeline"` *(This creates the actual "Save State")*
  
  
    Go back to the empty GitHub repository page you created in Step 1. Look for the section titled **"…or push an existing repository from the command line"**. 
    Copy the three lines of code they provide, paste them into your VS Code terminal, and press Enter. It will look something like this:
    ```cmd
    git remote add origin https://github.com/your-username/dopant-discovery-gnn.git
    git branch -M main
    git push -u origin main
    ```